Scope of the licence
--------------------
The MIT License in LICENSE covers the source code and documentation in this
repository. It does not cover the pack art: the textures and pack icons the
build produces, and the preview image(s) in docs/ (docs/enchanter-preview.png),
are derived from Mojang's Minecraft assets. Their use is governed by Mojang's
Minecraft Usage Guidelines (https://www.minecraft.net/en-us/usage-guidelines)
and the Minecraft EULA, not by the MIT License.

This repository contains no Mojang files. The build downloads the official
Minecraft client jar from Mojang at build time and derives the pack art from it.

The mobs pack takes nothing from the client jar. Its art is this project's own:
the illager-face textures (packs/mobs/files/assets/bettermodel/textures/
item/*_illager_face.png) and the Hopping Pig's texture (hopping_pig_vanilla_pig
.png, beside them) are original stand-ins, not copies of Mojang's. Its items
atlas (packs/mobs/files/assets/minecraft/atlases/items.json) contains no
pixels: it only references the vanilla textures minecraft:entity/illager/
pillager and minecraft:entity/pig/pig_temperate by name, which the player's own
client reads from its own assets at runtime. Its mushroom stem blockstate
(packs/mobs/files/assets/minecraft/blockstates/mushroom_stem.json) likewise
contains no pixels: it names the vanilla block models minecraft:block/
mushroom_stem and minecraft:block/mushroom_block_inside, read from the
player's own client, and this project's own moldy oak planks model. Since
0.13.0 its brown and red mushroom block blockstates likewise name only
minecraft:block/brown_mushroom_block, minecraft:block/red_mushroom_block,
minecraft:block/mushroom_block_inside and this project's own palm log and
fertilized sand models, and its petrified oak slab blockstate names only this
project's own palm slab and palm planks models.

